{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"surface","tool":"save_skill","arguments":{"name":"json-xs-compact-output","content":"# Compact JSON with json_xs\nUse for compacting JSON with this sandbox program. Check stored skills first.\nObserved: stdout reverses characters within each output line, including normal `-t json` output. Work around this by reversing the encoded JSON before printing.\nRun with argv [\"-f\", \"json\", \"-e\", \"print scalar(reverse(JSON::XS->new->utf8->encode($_))), \\\"\\\\n\\\"; exit\"] and pass original JSON as stdin. This parses the input and compactly encodes it, then counteracts the observed output reversal.\nCheck exit is 0, stderr empty, stdout parses as JSON equivalent to input, and trimmed stdout equals its compact JSON serialization and has one line. Tested successfully on nested arrays, a string, numbers and true. Recheck behavior in future sessions in case the program changes."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
